1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,026
Almost every long English word is a root with something attached at each end.

2
00:00:05,026 --> 00:00:06,328
Port means carry.

3
00:00:06,328 --> 00:00:08,229
Import: carry in.

4
00:00:08,229 --> 00:00:10,052
Export: carry out.

5
00:00:10,052 --> 00:00:12,408
Transport: carry across.

6
00:00:12,408 --> 00:00:14,687
Support: carry from under.

7
00:00:14,687 --> 00:00:16,875
Portable: able to be carried.

8
00:00:16,875 --> 00:00:20,247
And a reporter is one who carries back the news.

9
00:00:20,247 --> 00:00:23,372
Take the word apart and the meaning falls out.

10
00:00:23,372 --> 00:00:28,085
Prefixes change the meaning; suffixes change the part of speech.

